Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 09:00:07 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 4/5] Do not treat unlisted devices as incompatible

When com.mi.device.<Device> is missing, MiuiCamera falls back to the
generic com.mi.device.Common config but also sets a flag that makes
Camera.create2OpenCamera show the "Camera version isn't compatible"
dialog and finish. Clear that flag so devices like violet run with the
Common config.
---
 smali/OooO0OO/OooO0O0.smali | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/smali/OooO0OO/OooO0O0.smali b/smali/OooO0OO/OooO0O0.smali
index 01f8faa..cf0aac2 100644
--- a/smali/OooO0OO/OooO0O0.smali
+++ b/smali/OooO0OO/OooO0O0.smali
@@ -124,7 +124,7 @@
 
     invoke-direct {p0}, Lcom/mi/device/Common;-><init>()V
 
-    const/4 v0, 0x1
+    const/4 v0, 0x0
 
     .line 5
     sput-boolean v0, LOooO0OO/OooO0O0;->OooO00o:Z
